Package: datamonger
Title: Reproducible Retrieval and Decoding of Public Research Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(person(
      "Johan",
      "Larsson",
      email = "johan@jolars.co",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    ))
Description: Retrieves public research datasets through immutable registry
    selectors, verifies their exact bytes, and decodes them according to
    versioned, cross-language contracts. Decoded logical values are verified
    against canonical digests so that R, Python, and Julia clients can agree.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://datamonger.dev, https://github.com/jolars/datamonger
BugReports: https://github.com/jolars/datamonger/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    curl,
    digest,
    filelock,
    jsonlite,
    Matrix,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder:
    knitr
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo >= 1.82.0, rustc >= 1.82.0, xz
